<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gunakamadeva</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gunakamadeva was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu-valley">Kathmandu Valley</a> in the Thakuri period, traditionally placed in the 10th century. Later Nepalese chronicles credit him with founding the city of Kantipur, which became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu">Kathmandu</a>, and with establishing festivals and shrines there. His reign is known mainly from these chronicles rather than from contemporary records.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gunakamadeva.jpg" alt="Gunakamadeva" width="320" height="363" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Global Nepali Museum · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Gunakamadeva_of_Kathmandu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
